/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  solverDict -- the recycle plan.  Two cuts, both in the synthesis loop:
  the MATERIAL recycle (Recycle, the separator vapour going back) and the
  ENERGY recycle through the FEHE and the three kinetic beds, cut at
  PreheatedFeed, the FEHE's cold outlet that is bed 1's feed.  HotEffluent is
  the CONVERTER sector's outlet, and a tear cannot be declared on a sector's
  outlet by its plant label (the plan refuses it as an INLET TEAR), so the
  CONVERTER runs before the FEHE and the loop is cut where the FEHE closes
  it (DEV.md 4c C69).  The recycle tolerance is 1e-10: a tear at a REACTOR's
  inlet hands the bed the seed while the energy report reads the FEHE's
  produced stream, so bed 1's own first law shows the tear residual, and it
  must sit under the report's 1e-6 kW floor for a unit with no duty.  The
  tolerance's history is in README.md, "History".
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
tearStreams        ( Recycle  PreheatedFeed );
recycleSolver       Newton;
recycleTol          1e-10;
recycleMaxIter      200;
